-- title:
--   A unique transversal branch over t at each maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian integrally closed local domain with fraction field $K$, let $S$ be an integrally closed domain that is a finite free $R$-algebra with fraction field $F$, and let $F/K$ be separable, all compatibilities being expressed by the scalar-tower and fraction-field instances. Let $\varpi, t \in R$ with $\varpi \neq 0$, assume the maximal ideal of $R$ is the ideal generated by $\varpi$ and $t$, that $(\varpi)$ is prime with $R/(\varpi)$ a discrete valuation ring, and that $(t)$ is prime with $R/(t)$ of characteristic zero; assume moreover that $S/\varpi S$ is a Dedekind domain. Let $x \subseteq S$ be a maximal ideal, and suppose $R \to S$ is unramified at every prime $\mathfrak{Q} \leq x$ of height $1$ with $t \notin \mathfrak{Q}$ (the image of $t$ in $S$ being meant throughout). Then there exists a prime $\mathfrak{Q}$ of $S$ with $\mathfrak{Q} \leq x$, containing the image of $t$ and not containing the image of $\varpi$, such that for every local ring $\mathcal{O}$ which is an $S$-algebra realising the localisation of $S$ at $x$ one has $\mathfrak{Q}\mathcal{O} + \varpi\mathcal{O} = \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$; and $\mathfrak{Q}$ is the only prime below $x$ containing the image of $t$ and avoiding the image of $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the local core of the statement that, over a two-dimensional regular base with parameters $(\varpi, t)$, a finite free normal cover with Dedekind special fibre which is unramified away from $t$ carries exactly one branch through each closed point over $t = 0$, meeting the fibre $\varpi = 0$ transversally. It is the local input to [`Algebra.existsUnique_prime_le_map_sup_span_eq_maximalIdeal_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_isDedekindDomain_quotient`](thm.html#Algebra.existsUnique_prime_le_map_sup_span_eq_maximalIdeal_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_isDedekindDomain_quotient), and its proof combines a bound on the different along $t$, a bound on the different of the special fibre, and the factoriality of $S_x$ supplied by [`IsLocalRing.uniqueFactorizationMonoid_of_isPrincipalIdealRing_quotient`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.uniqueFactorizationMonoid_of_isPrincipalIdealRing_quotient).
